  "decisions": [
    "Repair the stale HighVariable name caches at the tail of the naming pass rather than relaxing `resolve_default_name_override`'s whole-symbol gate. The gate is a faithful port of C++'s `sym->isNameUndefined() && high->getSymbolOffset() < 0`; relaxing it would move when a Symbol consumes `base` and renumber every later local in any function where a partial high precedes its whole-cover sibling.",
    "Run the tail AFTER the spacebase attach pass. Running the catch-all before it would give previously-unnamed Symbols a name in time for `link_symbol_reference`'s `is_name_undefined` bail to stop firing, turning suppressed `&symbol` references into `&vN` renders -- a separable behaviour change. Last keeps every `&symbol` render byte-identical.",
    "Match on the placeholder shape (`Symbol::is_name_undefined`: len==15 && starts_with(\"$$undef\")) rather than re-reading the Symbol name for every high. A blanket re-read would overwrite names bound by the proto-partial, global and dynamic-symbol paths; the shape match can only ever replace a string that is not a valid C identifier.",
    "Rewrite the NAME only. The in-symbol offset and symbol type were bound from the same SymbolEntry the re-query returns, so re-setting them is a no-op and leaving them alone keeps the change provably scoped.",
    "No option: AGENTS.md's 'a strict bug fix that only corrects wrong output needs no flag'. Confirmed by the ablation (0/675) rather than assumed.",
    "CORRECTION to the triage's prediction: the duplicate declaration is NOT folded by DIV-52's `collapse_symbol_decls` (which is gated on `dedupvardecls`), but by the older ungated `is_scalar_partial_piece` guard in printc.rs, which skips a strict partial of a scalar mapped Symbol when a whole-cover sibling OF THE SAME NAME exists. Verified by running pass 2 with `option dedupvardecls off`: the fold still happens."
  ],
  "instrumentation_note": "`kuna decompile` shells out to decomp_dbg with stderr PIPED, so engine-level eprintln instrumentation is invisible on that path; the in-process `kuna decompile-all` path is the one to instrument. The refuter's non-perturbing discriminator is the --json `variables` array (extract_variables reads the ScopeLocal Symbol table directly); the console `rename` command perturbs (it also deletes the stack-canary locals).",
